# Ignore everything in this directory
*

# Except .gitignore and dotenv file
!.gitignore
!.env
!.env.secrets.example

# Secret files consumed via compose `secrets:`. Real values stay ignored
# by the blanket `*` above; only the .example templates are committed.
!secrets/
secrets/*
!secrets/*.example

# Jellyfin generates the rest of its config tree on first run and owns it
# thereafter: config/network.xml itself holds the real <CertificatePassword>
# once bootstrap seeds and patches it, and config/data/jellyfin.db holds
# users, devices, and playback history. network.xml.example is the one
# template here (BaseUrl/EnableHttps/CertificatePath/KnownProxies pre-set so
# Jellyfin's genuine first boot already reads the right values; confirmed
# live that Jellyfin preserves a pre-seeded network.xml byte for byte
# instead of overwriting it, same as every other app's seeded config).
!config/
config/*
!config/network.xml.example
